#: includes/abilities.php:205
msgid "The media library could not be read on this site. This is a condition on the site, not a problem with the request, so repeating the call unchanged will not help; the details are in the site error log."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: comma-separated rejected keys, 2: comma-separated accepted keys.
#: includes/abilities.php:366
#, php-format
msgid "Unknown input key: %1$s. This ability accepts: %2$s. A key it does not declare is never read, so the request would be answered as though that key had not been sent."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:503
msgid "The input has to be an object, for example {\"per_page\": 50}. Both parameters are optional; calling this ability with no input at all returns the first page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:654
msgid "List images with no usable alt text"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:655
msgid "Returns the image attachments for which this plugin has nothing to inject into a rendered image block, because the attachment carries no usable alt text. This plugin overwrites an image block's alt attribute with the attachment's alt text at render time, so the attachment is the single source of truth: setting the alt text once fixes every block that uses that image, with no post to re-save. Values that look set but are not are included and named: a single \"0\", and text consisting only of spaces, are both treated as absent by the injection."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:669
msgid "Page number, starting at 1."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:675
msgid "Images per page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:686
msgid "How many image attachments have no usable alt text."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:687
msgid "The page that was returned."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:688
msgid "The page size that was applied after clamping."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:689
msgid "Number of pages available."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:690
msgid "How many image attachments exist in scope altogether, so \"total\" can be read as a proportion. Counts attachments with an image MIME type whose status is inherit or publish; trashed and private ones are out of scope."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:691
msgid "Locale this answer was read in."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:694
msgid "The images on the requested page, newest first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:698
msgid "Attachment ID. This is what the alt text has to be set on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:699
msgid "Attachment title. Frequently the file name with the extension removed, and NOT a substitute for alt text."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:700
msgid "File name of the original upload."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:701
msgid "URL of the original file."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:702
msgid "MIME type of the attachment."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:703
msgid "What is stored today, verbatim. Empty for most, but not all: see \"reason\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:706
msgid "Why nothing would be injected. \"no_row\" when no alt text was ever saved; \"empty\" when an empty value is stored; \"whitespace_only\" when the stored text is only spaces; \"zero\" when the stored text is the single character 0, which PHP treats as empty and this plugin therefore skips; \"not_text\" when a serialised array, object or other non-text value is stored, which was written by code rather than in the media library."
msgstr ""

